    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule following the existing conventions for business-rule conflicts in this codebase (which already handled `DuplicateTelephoneException` and `DuplicateHouseholdException` the same way):\n\n1. **`CityCapacityExceededException`** (new, in the `service` package) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring the existing duplicate-exception classes, signaling a conflict rather than a bad request.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`** \u2014 added a guard that rejects creation when the city already holds `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` (50) or more owners. It reuses the single existing `ownerRepository.countByCity(...)` call (previously only used for the customer code) rather than querying twice, and I introduced a named constant for the limit.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps the new exception to **409 Conflict**, using the same `ProblemDetail` construction and logging pattern as the neighboring handlers.\n\nEach piece sits where it belongs: the rule in the service layer, the HTTP mapping in the advice, and the conflict signal in its own small exception class \u2014 no logic duplicated or piled into a catch-all.",
